# Shared agent instructions

Do **not** duplicate full policy here. Before non-trivial work, read:

1. `.agents/instructions/karpathy-guidelines.md` — coding discipline
2. `.agents/instructions/judgment-rubrics.md` — done / stuck / escalate / ask
3. `.agents/instructions/project-guidelines.md` — stack, git, deploy, language
4. `.agents/instructions/agent-tooling-guardrails.md` — MCP-first browser; no silent E2E deps

Then consult **`.agents/README.md`** — it maps every other instruction file
to its trigger (decisions, handoff, model dispatch, loops, issues,
methodology sync).

When **resuming**, read `docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md` first.

The three entry points (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, this file) must name the
**same** core list; if you change one, change all three.

## Quick rules

- Respond in **Traditional Chinese (繁體中文)** unless the user asks for another language (also set in `project-guidelines.md`).
- Communication language, stack, and deploy specifics are defined in `.agents/instructions/project-guidelines.md` — read it, don't assume.
- Read `docs/CURRENT_STATUS.md` and roadmap docs before large changes.
- Do not add Playwright or similar to `package.json` without explicit user approval.
- For Zeabur ops: load Zeabur skills when configured in project-guidelines.
